    "value": "Here’s a summary focused on ESLint 9.29.0 (and v9.x) breaking changes for `@eslint/js` \"recommended\" config, specifically highlighting the new `no-useless-assignment` rule and other relevant updates:\n\n### Major Breaking Changes in ESLint 9.x (`@eslint/js`)\n\n1. **Updated `eslint:recommended`**:\n   - The set of rules included in `\"eslint:recommended\"` has changed. New rules (such as `no-useless-assignment`) are now part of the recommended set, while some older or less important rules have been removed【3:5†source】【3:9†source】.\n\n2. **New Rule – `no-useless-assignment`**:\n   - **Purpose**: This rule flags when a variable is assigned a value that is never used (i.e., the assignment is “useless”).\n   - **Example**:\n     ```js\n     let id = 1234;  // 1234 is never used\n     id = calculateId(); // Only this assignment is actually needed\n     ```\n   - **Impact**: If you use `\"eslint:recommended\"` or turn on this rule, you may see new errors for cases where you assign a value to a variable that is later overwritten without being used【3:5†source】【3:9†source】.\n\n3. **Flat Config Is Now Default**:\n   - ESLint now uses the new flat config format by default (`eslint.config.js` or `eslint.config.mjs`). Legacy `.eslintrc.*` files are deprecated (though still supported if you opt in with an environment variable). Plugins and integrations should update to support flat config; mixed usage is discouraged【3:1†source】【3:5†source】【3:9†source】.\n\n4. **Node.js Version Requirement**:\n   - Node.js versions \u003c v18.18.0 and v19.x are no longer supported by ESLint 9.x【3:1†source】【3:9†source】.\n\n5. **Formatter Changes**:\n   - Only a handful of built-in formatters (stylish, html, json, json-with-meta) remain. Others (checkstyle, junit, tap, etc.) have been removed and must be installed separately if needed【3:5†source】【3:9†source】.\n\n### Notes \u0026 Migration\n\n- If using recommended configs, expect **new warnings or errors** after upgrading, mostly driven by new rules like `no-useless-assignment`.\n- You may need to update config files to the new flat config and check your Node version before upgrading.\n- Some previously allowed code patterns may now be errors due to new/updated rules in the recommended set.\n\n### Reference\n\n- [Official ESLint v9.0.0 release notes, including the introduction of `no-useless-assignment`](https://eslint.org/blog/2024/04/eslint-v9.0.0-released/)【3:9†source】\n- [Details on config migration and breaking changes](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/migration-guide-to-9.0.0)【3:1†source】\n\nIf you want a sample or further examples of what the `no-useless-assignment` rule catches, let me know!",
